      "question": {
        ":question/id": "47298a40-da64-5a82-a164-2fd4eb2721f1",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Consider a $12\\times 10$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=5,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =10 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+5 & =10 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =10-5 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "8062b4ea-20c2-596c-82c5-ef854c965029",
